<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mangalore</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mangaluru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mangalore (Mangaluru) is a port city on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the mouth of the Netravati and Gurupura rivers. It was a capital of the Alupa dynasty and a trading port visited by Arab and later Portuguese merchants. Contested by the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> and the British in the 18th century, it gave its name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-mangalore">Treaty of Mangalore</a> of 1784.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mangalore.jpg" alt="Mangalore" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Znyk · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Growing_skylines_of_the_Mangalore_CBD_region.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
